<p>Before movies could be delivered to the home on demand, Mandan residents left their living rooms to experience entertainment in person. During the early twentieth century, particularly the 1910s and 1920s, people from across the community attended theaters first for live vaudeville and variety acts and later for moving pictures.</p>

