<p>In 1909, the Topic Theatre, one block west of the {% place "inter-ocean-hotel" %}InterOcean Hotel{% endplace %}, installed an electric sign advertising its nightly variety shows. Moving pictures were accompanied by the local Imperial Orchestra. Other performers included {% person "fredric-the-great-magician" %}Fredric, the Great Magician{% endperson %}; {% person "miss-lamable" %}Miss LaMable, the Great Serpentine Dancer{% endperson %}; and {% person "jack-symonds" %}Jack Symonds, the Tramp Monologist{% endperson %}.</p>

<p>The Topic, at 504 West Main Street, opened as a live-entertainment venue and was later renamed the Family Theater. Frank Gilbreath assumed management from Edwin H. Wuerst and Paul R. Foster in early 1914. Harry L. Hartman purchased the building late that year and added a movie screen in 1915 as motion pictures grew in popularity.</p>
